Gotcha, deriving Hash / PartialEq / Eq are safe because we always construct JsString from marked strings or by calling `from_code_units`.

It feels a bit dangerous keeping this as a pub enum since there's nothing stopping a caller from manually creating `JsStrings` without enforcing the unpaired surrogate <--> wtf16 invariant. What do you think about exposing string refs? something like
```
pub struct JsString(Repr);

enum Repr {
    Utf8(String),
    Wtf16(Vec<u16>),
}

pub enum JsStringRef<'a> {
    Utf8(&'a str),
    Wtf16(&'a [u16]),
}

impl JsString {
    pub fn from_code_units(u: &[u16]) -> Self { /* canonicalizes */ }
    pub fn view(&self) -> JsStringRef<'_> { /* &self.0 → borrowed view */ }
    // ...
}
```
